# Current quiet-floor proposal review — source only

The frozen floor patch still replays exactly against the current art builder and environment manifest. No concrete new code defect was found in this narrow source review. The old recommendation for a separate import job is incorrect for this proposal: the reused tile already has a current imported resource, and the only prospective changes are text in an existing script/class and its provenance JSON. This review does not parse, import, apply, render or execute the candidate. All existing proposals, archives and the owner’s 383 recorded Save-job inputs remain untouched.

## Exact paired proposal and current inputs

The actual script is `scripts/acts/act1/mushroom_grotto_art.gd` (the owner’s `mushroom_art.gd` shorthand is not a separate target). In-memory unified-diff replay matched all four script hunks and the one manifest hunk without offsets or altered context. The output bytes equal the already frozen script and manifest candidates. The candidate JSON parses; all pre-existing manifest values remain exactly equal and the only appended key is `quiet_floor_overlay_preparation`.

