## Minimal next native checks after owner promotion

Use the next already-planned normal-route portrait as the affected rendering check; no separate broad campaign/import suite is suggested solely for the floor. Capture representative native room views through the same complete source/cue/Hero guard, retaining all eight Crossed source silhouettes when that room is active and both blocked/open court states. Check ordinary warning/active/recovery and actual landing/primary frames already produced by that fixture for: floor continuity/seams/flicker, full body/feet and contact shadow, yellow lane + reachable safe landing, harmless broken field perimeter and available/active/spent low cluster contrast, native HUD readability, and no new art occlusion. Hide the public Pause overlay only at the supported paused capture barrier and restore it before real GUI Resume; numeric camera success alone is insufficient. Do not change caps/camera/cue colors or physical tolerances to compensate for a floor failure.

At one existing quiet barrier add directly affected, atomic retained-resource negatives only: mutate each new threshold/AA mode/edge/blend/depth setting independently; hide/detach/translate the actual plane; replace its mesh/material/texture with an equivalent resource; and restore each original value/reference without repairing physics. Require nonempty `binding_error`, unchanged Hero/actor/Scheduler/native units/events during pure checks, INF/denied public framing as applicable, and empty/rejected full capture/preflight before any saved unit commits. Existing original control must recover exactly after each presentation-only restoration. These verify the new guard’s reach; no whole Save acceptance is inferred from a pure negative.

Any later recorder/source gates must consciously record the exact new builder2c428ad… and append-only manifestf5e5c203… rather than relabel the live job or auto-learn expectations. The unchanged tile is already in the current recorded set. No new bitmap/native UID is implied. Root remains responsible for promotion, native validation, visual review and acceptance.

